KG42.register("clusters-d0446f75459c6052c8d8b3f7",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v142-d-CL006","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","label":"Cournot supply-quantity pricing and baseline purchase-price assumptions","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL006","label":"Cournot supply-quantity pricing and baseline purchase-price assumptions","market_meaning":"In the Cournot benchmark with seller prosumers as players, the internal selling price is determined by the microgrid PV supply quantity and external price endpoints, and the fixed internal purchase-price assumption in the reported comparison is retained. Pricing under the excess-supply region and under zero demand has not yet been closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["pricing","bidding","participation"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"R014 and R015 both belong to M03; shared R012 only limits the player scope and does not constitute an additional execution dependency for pricing. The fixed purchase price is retained as a comparison assumption. The applicability domains of the linear selling price and the sufficient-supply price floor have not been unified, and this is not merged with the strict buy-sell price ordering or same-named price quantities of M01.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The product description and supply-quantity pricing have a direct functional connection and jointly define the quotation rule under given supply; independent player eligibility is primarily owned by CL005. This cluster does not claim to include Cournot endogenous supply or a complete Nash equilibrium solution.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the relationship from supply quantity to selling price, the endpoint parameters, and the purchase-price assumption for the comparison case, while retaining its unresolved applicability domain."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R015","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"States that the product on which the price relationship acts is the PV energy supplied within the microgrid."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Only cites seller-player eligibility to delimit the Cournot context; primary ownership is in CL005, and it adds neither a pricing dependency nor an independent rule count."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL006-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R015","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R015::V::product.local_energy","v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::V::product.local_energy","v141-c-R014::x::var_es","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"],"rationale":"The product chain describes the supplied PV energy, and the pricing chain uses its total supply as the selling-price input; R015 has no independent quantity object, and no quantity-identity mapping is fabricated."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL006-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"],"rationale":"The same passage of the source text limits the seller players and gives the supply-price relationship, supporting a shared Cournot interpretation scope; this is shared context and does not add a requires edge from player eligibility to pricing."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL006-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R014::V::product.local_energy","v141-c-R015::V::product.local_energy"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R014::V::product.local_energy","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the same PV energy product supplied by the Cournot microgrid; only a display entry is selected, and it is not merged across mechanisms with the per-prosumer net-energy object of M01."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"When E^b is positive and the import price is higher than the export price, the existing linear formula continues to decrease after E^s exceeds E^b, and this cannot simultaneously hold unconditionally with the provision that the selling price is fixed at λ^s under sufficient supply.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should clarify whether the linear segment is domain-limited and whether there is another price floor or piecewise rule; D does not itself add a truncated expression."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The slope definition uses E^b as the denominator, but the zero-demand case and the effective demand domain are not specified; when zero demand and zero supply coexist, the two price-endpoint conditions may also conflict.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::theta::par_eb","v141-c-R014::theta::par_b","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify applicable conditions such as nonzero demand, or have a sourced upstream rule handle the zero-demand degenerate case."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing chains do not express the endogenous supply quantity determined by seller utility, optimal consumption, and their mutual influence. Eqs. (33)-(35) in B cannot be directly added by D into frozen C, so here only candidate pricing under a given supply quantity can be provided.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R014","v141-c-R015"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::x::var_es","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R015::phi::v141-c-R015-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If complete Cournot clearing rules are required, C should supplement the endogenous supply solution as well as feasible roots, consumption domain, and equilibrium conditions; these missing contents are not to be regarded as already covered by the existing pricing chains."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL006-G004","category":"unverified_source","description":"The Cournot formula, the sufficient-supply statement, and the fixed purchase-price assumption are all unaudited candidate sources. The fixed purchase price is retained as λ^s according to the original text and is not changed to λ^b because of its profitability explanation or because it differs from the price ordering of other mechanisms.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R012","v141-c-R014","v141-c-R015"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::theta::par_pb","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the appendix pricing domain and the case purchase-price assumption; if MGO profitability is to be evaluated, M03's own accounting basis must be supplied, and M01 profit rules cannot be directly reused."}]},"rule_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R014","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R015","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R012"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-09e23646758c214d","COMP-34f4647dbfb7e00c","COMP-52f5faebc827833c","COMP-a66dbdae6253f618"]});
